    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d4">

                <pb facs="0116" n="4" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg4"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/1369: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-01-08T10:00:00+09:00">January 8, 1935—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 8—4:32 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3. The Soviet Ambassador<anchor n="8" xml:id="d4-f1"/> told me last night that
                    the press reports of an early settlement of the sale of the Chinese Eastern
                    Railway are unfounded and have been announced from Japanese sources merely to
                    strengthen Hirota’s<anchor n="9" xml:id="d4-f2"/> position in the forthcoming
                    sessions of the Diet. Some slight advance has been made in the negotiations but
                    the question of guarantees of payment is still unsettled.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d4-f1" n="8" xml:id="d4-f1-content">
